# Env files.
#
# `.env` is deliberately COMMITTED during development: it holds only the public
# Supabase URL + publishable (anon) key, which RLS gates and which already ship
# in the browser bundle. That keeps `git clone && npm i && npm run dev` working
# with no setup, locally and in CI.
#
# Secrets live in `.env.local`, which stays ignored — above all
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, which bypasses RLS entirely. Also STRIPE_SECRET_KEY,
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET, LOVABLE_API_KEY, SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD, CLOUDINARY_URL
# and the E2E credentials. See .env.local.example.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.local.example

